Hello, a new version of poppr has been released this week.

This version of poppr introduces the function bootgen2genind() that allows you to use aboot()with distance functions that explicitly expect "genind" objects (type ?aboot in your R console for details):

aboot(myData, dist = myDist) # fails
aboot(myData, dist = function(x) myDist(bootgen2genind(x))) # works

There are other various bug fixes and improvements, which are listed at https://github.com/grunwaldlab/poppr/releases/tag/v.2.3.0

Cheers,

Zhian

